IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ltcs-dates`

-- Motor Accidents (Lifetime Care and Support) Act 2006 (NSW) -- Parts 1, 2, 2A, 3 and 4 (who the Act reaches, who may
-- join the Lifetime Care and Support Scheme and for how long, what the Authority pays for, and the disputes), from the
-- seat of the person injured in a motor accident.
--
-- SEAT: the person who suffered the motor accident injury (or a parent, guardian or other person acting for them), who
-- is or may become a "participant in the Scheme". Every exported question is one that person would ask: "Does the Act
-- apply to my injury?", "Am I eligible?", "Who can apply for me?", "Must the Authority accept me?", "Until when am I an
-- interim participant?", "Does my time limit for suing stop running?", "Will the Authority pay for this?", "Where does my
-- dispute go, and by when?", "Must I do what the assessor asks?", "Who pays my legal costs?". The Authority, the
-- assessors, the panels and the Personal Injury Commission get no seat: what they do is encoded as what it means for the
-- injured person. The owner or driver of an uninsured vehicle, from whom s 54 lets the Authority recover, has a seat of
-- their own in ltcs-seat-owner-driver.l4.
--
-- Provisions: ss 3, 4, 5A (definitions and application); ss 7, 7A, 7B, 8, 9, 11 (participation); ss 11A, 11AA, 11B,
-- 11C (payments); ss 14, 15, 17, 18, 20, 21 (disputes about eligibility and about motor accident injury); ss 23-25, 27,
-- 29 (treatment and care needs assessment); in comments only: s 8(3)-(6), s 11(1), s 11A(4), s 25(5), Schedule 3 cl 2.
-- Out, with reasons in NOTES.md (which has the full list): machinery and spent provisions (among them ss 16 and 26,
-- final and binding effect); Parts 5, 6 and 7 apart from s 54 (payments to hospitals and providers, the Authority, its
-- funding).
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no question answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no (a "means" or "are"
-- definition, a condition introduced by "if", "only if", "while" or "but only on", a flat "cannot" or "not"), or NOTHING
-- where the Act does not answer on the facts given; each NOTHING carries a "NOTHING-kind" comment. Answers that are
-- enumerations carry a constructor for "the Act does not say" where that can arise.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025; version as at 1 July 2021; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Motor Accidents (Lifetime Care and Support) Act 2006`

§§ `The nouns`

-- How the Act reaches the injury (ss 4, 7A, 7B).
DECLARE `How the Act reaches my injury` IS ONE OF
    `the Act applies to my injury`
    `the Act does not apply, but I may buy in because the accident was before the Scheme began (s 7A)`
    `the Act does not apply, but I may buy in because the accident was outside New South Wales (s 7B)`
    `the Act does not say whether I may buy in for an accident both outside New South Wales and before the Scheme began`
    `the Act does not apply to my injury`

-- Which eligibility criteria in the LTCS Guidelines (s 7(1), (2)) the injury meets: the Guidelines, not the Act, set
-- them, so this is asked.
DECLARE `The LTCS Guidelines criteria my injury meets` IS ONE OF
    `the criteria for lifetime participation`
    `the criteria for interim participation only`
    `neither`

DECLARE `My eligibility to participate` IS ONE OF
    `I am eligible as a lifetime participant`
    `I am eligible as an interim participant`
    `I am eligible as a lifetime participant if I buy in by paying the contribution the Authority determines`
    `I am not eligible`
    `the Act does not say whether I am eligible`

-- Who is applying (s 8(1)).
DECLARE `Who is applying` IS ONE OF
    `I am, or someone is applying on my behalf`
    `the insurer of a claim I made for the injury`
    `someone else`

-- What the Authority is satisfied of (s 9).
DECLARE `What the Authority is satisfied of` IS ONE OF
    `that I am eligible as a lifetime participant`
    `that I am eligible as an interim participant`
    `that I am not eligible`

DECLARE `What the Authority must do with my application` IS ONE OF
    `it must accept me as a lifetime participant`
    `it must accept me as an interim participant`
    `it cannot accept me as an interim participant again`
    `the Act does not require it to accept me`
    `the Act does not say`

DECLARE `My participation on the day` IS ONE OF
    `I am a lifetime participant, for life`
    `I am an interim participant`
    `my interim participation has ended`
    `I am not a participant`

-- The time limit asked about (s 11(2)).
DECLARE `The time limit for my damages claim` IS ONE OF
    `section 109 of the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999`
    `a provision of the Limitation Act 1969`
    `another time limit, for example under the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017`

-- The kinds of treatment and care need in s 5A(1).
DECLARE `The kind of treatment or care` IS ONE OF
    `medical treatment, including pharmaceuticals`
    `dental treatment`
    `rehabilitation`
    `ambulance transportation`
    `respite care`
    `attendant care services`
    `aids and appliances`
    `prostheses`
    `education and vocational training`
    `home and transport modification`
    `workplace and educational facility modifications`
    `a kind prescribed by the regulations`
    `something else`

DECLARE `What the Authority must do about this expense` IS ONE OF
    `the Authority must pay the reasonable expense`
    `the Authority is not required to pay, but may elect to because it is of the opinion that special circumstances justify it`
    `the Authority is not required to pay`
    `no expense is payable for it`
    `the Act does not say`

DECLARE `What my dispute is about` IS ONE OF
    `whether my injury meets the eligibility criteria in the LTCS Guidelines`
    `whether my injury is a motor accident injury`
    `the Authority's assessment of my treatment and care needs`
    `something else`

DECLARE `Where my dispute goes` IS ONE OF
    `to an Assessment Panel of 3 assessors, referred by me, the insurer or the Authority (s 14)`
    `to the Personal Injury Commission, referred by the Authority at my request (s 20)`
    `to an assessor, referred by the Authority if I ask within 28 days after its certificate (s 24)`
    `the Act sets no dispute process for it`

DECLARE `The proceeding my legal costs are for` IS ONE OF
    `a dispute about eligibility before an Assessment Panel or Review Panel`
    `a dispute about whether my injury is a motor accident injury`
    `an assessment of my treatment and care needs, or a dispute or review about it`
    `something else`

DECLARE `The cost of attending a panel` IS ONE OF
    `my travel and accommodation to attend the panel`
    `the travel and accommodation of a parent or carer who goes with me`
    `some other cost`

-- The parties and acts of the two regulative rules (ss 24(2), 25(2)).
DECLARE `Scheme party` IS ONE OF `the participant`, `the Authority`
DECLARE `Scheme act` IS ONE OF
    `ask the Authority to refer the dispute to an assessor`
    `refer the assessor's determination for review`

§§ `ss 3, 4 -- the relevant Scheme commencement date, and the motor accident injuries the Act applies to`

-- s 3(1) "relevant Scheme commencement date ... means (a) 1 October 2006 if the person was under 16 years of age at the
-- time of the motor accident that caused the injuries, or (b) 1 October 2007 in any other case."
GIVEN `the birthday` IS A DATE, `the accident day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the relevant Scheme commencement date for someone born on` `the birthday` `injured on` `the accident day` MEANS
    IF `the age of someone born on` `the birthday` `on` `the accident day` LESS THAN 16
    THEN `the date` 1 10 2006
    ELSE `the date` 1 10 2007

@export What is my relevant Scheme commencement date: the date from which the Lifetime Care and Support Scheme covers motor accidents that injure me (s 3(1))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident in which you were injured
GIVETH A DATE
`What is my relevant Scheme commencement date` MEANS
    `the relevant Scheme commencement date for someone born on` `my date of birth` `injured on` `the day of the accident`

-- s 3(1) "motor accident injury means injury caused by a motor accident" ("motor accident" is borrowed from the Motor
-- Accidents Compensation Act 1999 by s 5, and asked). s 4(1) "applies only in respect of motor accident injuries ...
-- as a result of a motor accident occurring on or after the relevant Scheme commencement date"; s 4(2) "applies only in
-- respect of motor accident injuries resulting from motor accidents occurring in New South Wales"; s 4(3) "only if
-- there is a motor vehicle involved ... that has motor accident insurance cover for the motor accident (within the
-- meaning of section 3B of the [1999 Act])". s 4(4): fault does not matter, so fault is not asked. s 7A(1): a
-- pre-commencement injury "may be accepted as a lifetime participant ... if the person pays"; s 7A(3)(a) only if the
-- person would have been eligible had the accident occurred immediately after the relevant Scheme commencement date.
-- s 7B(1): the same for an accident "outside New South Wales"; s 7B(3)(a) had it occurred in New South Wales. The
-- counterfactual moves only the date (s 7A) or the place (s 7B), so s 4(3)'s insured vehicle is still needed (fork F1).
-- An accident both before the date and outside NSW meets neither counterfactual alone (fork F2).
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE, `the day of the accident` IS A DATE, `the injury was caused by a motor accident` IS A BOOLEAN, `the accident happened in New South Wales` IS A BOOLEAN, `an insured vehicle was involved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `How the Act reaches my injury`
`the reach of the Act` `my date of birth` `the day of the accident` `the injury was caused by a motor accident` `the accident happened in New South Wales` `an insured vehicle was involved` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the injury was caused by a motor accident`) THEN `the Act does not apply to my injury`
           IF (NOT `an insured vehicle was involved`) THEN `the Act does not apply to my injury`
           IF `the accident happened in New South Wales` AND (NOT `before the Scheme`) THEN `the Act applies to my injury`
           IF `the accident happened in New South Wales` THEN `the Act does not apply, but I may buy in because the accident was before the Scheme began (s 7A)`
           IF (NOT `before the Scheme`) THEN `the Act does not apply, but I may buy in because the accident was outside New South Wales (s 7B)`
           OTHERWISE `the Act does not say whether I may buy in for an accident both outside New South Wales and before the Scheme began`
    WHERE
        `before the Scheme` MEANS `the day of the accident` `is before` (`the relevant Scheme commencement date for someone born on` `my date of birth` `injured on` `the day of the accident`)

@export Does the Lifetime Care and Support Act apply to my motor accident injury, or could I buy into the Scheme (ss 3, 4, 7A, 7B)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident in which you were injured
      `the injury was caused by a motor accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury was caused by a motor accident (an accident involving the use or operation of a motor vehicle, as the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999 defines it)
      `the accident happened in New South Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident happened in New South Wales
      `an insured vehicle was involved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at least one motor vehicle involved in the accident had NSW compulsory third-party (motor accident insurance) cover for the accident; it does not matter whether the others did, or who was at fault
GIVETH A `How the Act reaches my injury`
`Does the Act apply to my motor accident injury` MEANS
    `the reach of the Act` `my date of birth` `the day of the accident` `the injury was caused by a motor accident` `the accident happened in New South Wales` `an insured vehicle was involved`

§§ `s 7 -- eligibility to be a participant`

-- s 7(1) eligible "if the person's injury satisfies the criteria specified in the LTCS Guidelines"; s 7(2) lifetime or
-- interim; s 7(3) "not eligible ... if the person has been awarded damages, pursuant to a final judgment entered by a
-- court or a binding settlement, for future economic loss in respect of the treatment and care needs ... that relate to
-- the injury". ss 7A(3)(b), 7B(3)(b): for a buy-in, the damages are disregarded. s 7A(1), 7B(1): a buy-in is only as a
-- lifetime participant; for an injury that meets only the interim criteria the Act gives no route (fork F3).
GIVEN `the reach` IS A `How the Act reaches my injury`, `the criteria` IS A `The LTCS Guidelines criteria my injury meets`, `I have been awarded damages for future treatment and care` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My eligibility to participate`
`the eligibility for` `the reach` `the criteria` `I have been awarded damages for future treatment and care` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reach`
    WHEN `the Act does not apply to my injury` THEN `I am not eligible`
    WHEN `the Act does not say whether I may buy in for an accident both outside New South Wales and before the Scheme began` THEN `the Act does not say whether I am eligible`  -- NOTHING-kind (fork F2)
    WHEN `the Act applies to my injury` THEN
        IF `I have been awarded damages for future treatment and care`
        THEN `I am not eligible`
        ELSE CONSIDER `the criteria`
             WHEN `the criteria for lifetime participation` THEN `I am eligible as a lifetime participant`
             WHEN `the criteria for interim participation only` THEN `I am eligible as an interim participant`
             OTHERWISE `I am not eligible`
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `the criteria`
        WHEN `the criteria for lifetime participation` THEN `I am eligible as a lifetime participant if I buy in by paying the contribution the Authority determines`
        WHEN `the criteria for interim participation only` THEN `the Act does not say whether I am eligible`  -- NOTHING-kind (fork F3)
        OTHERWISE `I am not eligible`

@export Am I eligible to be a participant in the Lifetime Care and Support Scheme, as a lifetime or an interim participant (ss 4, 7, 7A, 7B)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor accident in which you were injured
      `the injury was caused by a motor accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury was caused by a motor accident (an accident involving the use or operation of a motor vehicle, as the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999 defines it)
      `the accident happened in New South Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accident happened in New South Wales
      `an insured vehicle was involved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at least one motor vehicle involved in the accident had NSW compulsory third-party (motor accident insurance) cover for the accident
      `the criteria my injury meets` IS A `The LTCS Guidelines criteria my injury meets` @desc Which eligibility criteria in the LTCS Guidelines your injury meets (decided by the Authority, or on a dispute by an Assessment Panel). One of: "the criteria for lifetime participation", "the criteria for interim participation only", "neither"
      `I have been awarded damages for future treatment and care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court's final judgment or a binding settlement has awarded you damages for future economic loss for the treatment and care needs that relate to this injury
GIVETH A `My eligibility to participate`
`Am I eligible to be a participant` MEANS
    `the eligibility for` (`the reach of the Act` `my date of birth` `the day of the accident` `the injury was caused by a motor accident` `the accident happened in New South Wales` `an insured vehicle was involved`) `the criteria my injury meets` `I have been awarded damages for future treatment and care`

§§ `s 8 -- who may apply`

-- s 8(1) an application "can only be made by or on behalf of the person or by the insurer of a claim made by the person
-- in respect of the injury"; ss 7A(4), 7B(4) a buy-in application "cannot be made by an insurer". s 8(2): an insurer's
-- application "does not require the consent of the person". In comments only: s 8(3) the State Insurance Regulatory
-- Authority may direct the insurer to apply (the insurer's duty); s 8(4) the application is in the approved form with its
-- particulars (asked as "duly made" in `Must the Authority accept me as a participant`); s 8(5) "The Authority may
-- require the injured person to provide authorisation for the Authority to obtain information and documents relevant to
-- the motor accident injury" (the Authority's power; the Act states no consequence if the person refuses); s 8(6) the
-- LTCS Guidelines may govern applications, including time limits for making them (not deposited).
@export Can this person or body apply for me to become a participant in the Scheme (ss 7A(4), 7B(4), 8(1), (2))? An insurer that may apply does not need my consent.
GIVEN `who is applying` IS A `Who is applying` @desc Who would make the application. One of: "I am, or someone is applying on my behalf", "the insurer of a claim I made for the injury", "someone else"
      `the application is to buy in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application is to buy in under section 7A (an accident before the Scheme began) or section 7B (an accident outside New South Wales)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can this person apply for me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who is applying`
    WHEN `I am, or someone is applying on my behalf` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the insurer of a claim I made for the injury` THEN
        IF `the application is to buy in` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 9 -- acceptance, and how long participation lasts`

-- s 9(2) "If the Authority is satisfied that a person is eligible ... and that application ... has been duly made, the
-- Authority must accept the person as a lifetime participant or an interim participant (according to the person's
-- eligibility)." s 9(3): an interim participant must be accepted as a lifetime participant when the Authority becomes
-- satisfied of lifetime eligibility; s 9(7): an expired interim participation does not prevent it. s 9(6) "A person
-- cannot be accepted as an interim participant more than once in relation to the same motor accident injury." ss 7A(1),
-- 7B(1): a buy-in "may be accepted as a lifetime participant ... if the person pays" the contribution (fork F4: once paid,
-- s 9(2) makes acceptance a duty). s 9(3) is a duty of its own: it turns on the Authority becoming satisfied "during the
-- person's interim participation", and, unlike s 9(2), it says nothing of an application, so no duly made application
-- is required for the step from interim to lifetime participation while the interim participation lasts (fork F14).
-- Once it has ended, s 9(7) leaves the way open but the duty is s 9(2)'s, with its application.
@export If I (or someone for me) apply to join the Scheme, or the Authority becomes satisfied during my interim participation that I am eligible for lifetime participation, must the Authority accept me, and as what (ss 7A(1), 7B(1), 9(2), (3), (6), (7))?
GIVEN `what the Authority is satisfied of` IS A `What the Authority is satisfied of` @desc What the Authority is satisfied of about your eligibility. One of: "that I am eligible as a lifetime participant", "that I am eligible as an interim participant", "that I am not eligible"
      `the application was duly made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application was made to the Authority in the approved form, with the required particulars, by someone allowed to make it
      `I have already been an interim participant for this injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already been accepted as an interim participant for the same motor accident injury (even if that participation has ended)
      `the application is to buy in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application is to buy in under section 7A (an accident before the Scheme began) or section 7B (an accident outside New South Wales)
      `I have paid the buy-in contribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid the Authority the contribution it determined for a buy-in (answer no if you are not buying in)
      `I am an interim participant now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an interim participant for this injury now, your interim participation not having ended
GIVETH A `What the Authority must do with my application`
`Must the Authority accept me as a participant` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `I am an interim participant now` AND `what the Authority is satisfied of` EQUALS `that I am eligible as a lifetime participant` THEN `it must accept me as a lifetime participant`
           IF (NOT `the application was duly made`) THEN `the Act does not require it to accept me`
           IF `what the Authority is satisfied of` EQUALS `that I am not eligible` THEN `the Act does not require it to accept me`
           IF `the application is to buy in` AND `what the Authority is satisfied of` EQUALS `that I am eligible as an interim participant` THEN `the Act does not say`
           IF `the application is to buy in` AND (NOT `I have paid the buy-in contribution`) THEN `the Act does not require it to accept me`
           IF `what the Authority is satisfied of` EQUALS `that I am eligible as a lifetime participant` THEN `it must accept me as a lifetime participant`
           IF `I have already been an interim participant for this injury` THEN `it cannot accept me as an interim participant again`
           OTHERWISE `it must accept me as an interim participant`

-- s 9(5) "A person 3 years of age or over who is accepted as an interim participant remains an interim participant for
-- a period of 2 years only." s 9(5A) "A person under 3 years of age who is accepted as an interim participant remains an
-- interim participant until the person is 5 years of age." Schedule 3 cl 2 extends s 9(5A) to those already interim
-- participants when it commenced. Fork F6: the 2 years include the day of acceptance, so the last day is the day before
-- the second anniversary; "until the person is 5" ends on the day before the fifth birthday. This counts differently from
-- the 28 days of ss 24(2) and 25(2) (fork F11), deliberately: s 9(1) makes the person a participant on the day of
-- acceptance, so that day is part of the period of participation that "remains" for 2 years, whereas "28 days after"
-- a certificate starts the day after it is given. The Interpretation Act 1987 s 36 reading (exclude the day of
-- acceptance, last day the second anniversary) is the other branch of F6.
GIVEN `the birthday` IS A DATE, `the day accepted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of interim participation for someone born on` `the birthday` `accepted on` `the day accepted` MEANS
    IF `the age of someone born on` `the birthday` `on` `the day accepted` LESS THAN 3
    THEN (`the day someone born on` `the birthday` `turns` 5) `plus days` (0 MINUS 1)
    ELSE (`the day accepted` `plus months` 24) `plus days` (0 MINUS 1)

@export If I am accepted as an interim participant, what is the last day of my interim participation (s 9(5), (5A))? Acceptance as a lifetime participant ends it earlier (s 9(5B)).
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day I was accepted as an interim participant` IS A DATE @desc The day the Authority accepted you in writing as an interim participant
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day of my interim participation` MEANS
    `the last day of interim participation for someone born on` `my date of birth` `accepted on` `the day I was accepted as an interim participant`

-- s 9(4) "A person accepted as a lifetime participant in the Scheme remains a participant for life." s 9(5B) an interim
-- participant accepted as a lifetime participant "ceases to be an interim participant on that acceptance".
GIVEN `the birthday` IS A DATE, `accepted as interim` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day accepted as interim` IS A DATE, `accepted as lifetime` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day accepted as lifetime` IS A DATE, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `My participation on the day`
`the participation of someone born on` `the birthday` `interim` `accepted as interim` `from` `the day accepted as interim` `lifetime` `accepted as lifetime` `from` `the day accepted as lifetime` `on` `the day` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `accepted as lifetime` AND (NOT (`the day` `is before` `the day accepted as lifetime`)) THEN `I am a lifetime participant, for life`
           IF (NOT `accepted as interim`) THEN `I am not a participant`
           IF `the day` `is before` `the day accepted as interim` THEN `I am not a participant`
           IF (`the last day of interim participation for someone born on` `the birthday` `accepted on` `the day accepted as interim`) `is before` `the day` THEN `my interim participation has ended`
           OTHERWISE `I am an interim participant`

@export Am I a participant in the Scheme on a given day, and as what (s 9(4), (5), (5A), (5B))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `I was accepted as an interim participant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority has accepted you as an interim participant for this injury
      `the day I was accepted as an interim participant` IS A DATE @desc The day you were accepted as an interim participant (any day if you were not)
      `I was accepted as a lifetime participant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority has accepted you as a lifetime participant for this injury
      `the day I was accepted as a lifetime participant` IS A DATE @desc The day you were accepted as a lifetime participant (any day if you were not)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about
GIVETH A `My participation on the day`
`Am I a participant on this day` MEANS
    `the participation of someone born on` `my date of birth` `interim` `I was accepted as an interim participant` `from` `the day I was accepted as an interim participant` `lifetime` `I was accepted as a lifetime participant` `from` `the day I was accepted as a lifetime participant` `on` `the day I am asking about`

§§ `s 11(2) -- the time limit for a damages claim while an interim participant`

-- s 11(2) "While a person is an interim participant in the Scheme in respect of an injury, time does not run for the
-- purposes of section 109 ... of the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999 or a provision of the Limitation Act 1969 in
-- respect of a cause of action on a claim for damages that relate to the injury or to any other injury suffered by the
-- person as a result of the motor accident concerned." Outside the "while", JUST FALSE. A time limit under another Act
-- (for example the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017, which s 11(2) does not name): NOTHING (finding 2). In a comment
-- only: s 11(1) "This Act does not limit or otherwise affect the application of the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999
-- in respect of a motor accident injury of a person who is or who is eligible to become a participant ..., except as
-- specifically provided by that Act" (the damages claim itself is under that Act, outside this encoding).
@export Does section 11(2) stop time running, on a given day, for my damages claim about the accident (s 11(2))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `I was accepted as an interim participant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority has accepted you as an interim participant for the injury
      `the day I was accepted as an interim participant` IS A DATE @desc The day you were accepted as an interim participant (any day if you were not)
      `I was accepted as a lifetime participant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority has accepted you as a lifetime participant for the injury
      `the day I was accepted as a lifetime participant` IS A DATE @desc The day you were accepted as a lifetime participant (any day if you were not)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about
      `the claim is for an injury from the same accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your damages claim relates to the injury for which you are a participant, or to another injury you suffered in the same motor accident
      `the time limit` IS A `The time limit for my damages claim` @desc The time limit you are asking about. One of: "section 109 of the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999", "a provision of the Limitation Act 1969", "another time limit, for example under the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does section 11(2) stop time running on my damages claim` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the time limit` EQUALS `another time limit, for example under the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 11(2) names only s 109 of the 1999 Act and the Limitation Act 1969)
           IF (NOT `the claim is for an injury from the same accident`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `my participation` EQUALS `I am an interim participant` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `my participation` MEANS `the participation of someone born on` `my date of birth` `interim` `I was accepted as an interim participant` `from` `the day I was accepted as an interim participant` `lifetime` `I was accepted as a lifetime participant` `from` `the day I was accepted as a lifetime participant` `on` `the day I am asking about`

-- The days on which time did not run, from the day of acceptance as an interim participant to the earliest of the last
-- day of interim participation, the day before acceptance as a lifetime participant, and the day asked about, counting
-- both ends (fork F8).
@export Up to a given day, on how many days has my interim participation stopped the time limit running for my damages claim (s 11(2))? They are added to the time limit under section 109 of the 1999 Act or the Limitation Act 1969.
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day I was accepted as an interim participant` IS A DATE @desc The day the Authority accepted you as an interim participant
      `I was accepted as a lifetime participant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority has since accepted you as a lifetime participant for the injury
      `the day I was accepted as a lifetime participant` IS A DATE @desc The day you were accepted as a lifetime participant (any day if you were not)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The last day to count up to (for example today)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many days has my interim participation stopped time running` MEANS
    `the larger of` 0 `and` ((`the days from` `the day I was accepted as an interim participant` `to` `the last day counted`) PLUS 1)
    WHERE
        `the interim last day` MEANS `the last day of interim participation for someone born on` `my date of birth` `accepted on` `the day I was accepted as an interim participant`
        `the end of interim` MEANS
            IF `I was accepted as a lifetime participant`
            THEN `the earlier of` `the interim last day` `and` (`the day I was accepted as a lifetime participant` `plus days` (0 MINUS 1))
            ELSE `the interim last day`
        `the last day counted` MEANS `the earlier of` `the end of interim` `and` `the day I am asking about`

§§ `Part 2A -- what the Authority pays for`

-- s 5A(1) the treatment and care needs "are the participant's needs for or in connection with any of the following"
-- (a)-(k), and (l) kinds prescribed by the regulations; s 5A(2) not those "declared by the regulations to be excluded".
-- s 11A(1) "The Authority is to pay for all of the reasonable expenses incurred by or on behalf of a person in relation to
-- the assessed treatment and care needs of the person while the person is a participant"; s 11A(2) assessed needs are
-- those the Authority assesses as reasonable and necessary and related to the injury; s 11A(3) "No expenses are payable
-- in respect of (a) excluded treatment and care needs, and (b) treatment and care needs that are not assessed".
-- s 11B(1) not required to pay for (a) anything provided "on a gratuitous basis" or (b) anything required to be provided
-- by an approved provider but provided by someone who is not one; s 11B(2) "may elect to make a payment ... if the
-- Authority is of the opinion that special circumstances exist". s 11C(1) attendant care services, and services the LTCS
-- Guidelines identify (other than a medical practitioner's), are to be provided only by an approved provider.
-- The regulations (excluded and prescribed kinds) and the Guidelines are not deposited: asked as facts. In a comment
-- only: s 11A(4) the Authority "may pay those expenses by the payment to the participant of an amount to cover those
-- expenses over a fixed period pursuant to an agreement between the Authority and the participant" (how, not whether,
-- the Authority pays; it needs the participant's agreement, so it is not something done to the participant).
@export Will the Lifetime Care and Support Authority pay for this treatment, care, support or service (ss 5A, 11A, 11B, 11C)?
GIVEN `the kind of treatment or care` IS A `The kind of treatment or care` @desc The kind of treatment or care. One of: "medical treatment, including pharmaceuticals", "dental treatment", "rehabilitation", "ambulance transportation", "respite care", "attendant care services", "aids and appliances", "prostheses", "education and vocational training", "home and transport modification", "workplace and educational facility modifications", "a kind prescribed by the regulations", "something else"
      `the regulations declare it excluded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations declare this kind of treatment or care to be an excluded treatment and care need
      `it is in my assessed treatment and care needs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority's treatment and care needs assessment (as revised after any dispute) includes it as reasonable and necessary and related to your motor accident injury
      `I was a participant when the expense was incurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a participant in the Scheme when the expense was incurred
      `the expense is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the amount of the expense is reasonable
      `it was provided free` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was provided gratuitously: you have not paid for it and are not liable to pay for it
      `the LTCS Guidelines require an approved provider for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the LTCS Guidelines say this kind of treatment or service must be provided by an approved provider (attendant care services always must)
      `it was provided by a medical practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was a medical practitioner's service
      `the provider was approved at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who provided it was an approved provider of it at the time
      `the Authority is of the opinion that special circumstances justify paying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Authority is of the opinion that special circumstances justify paying although it is not required to
GIVETH A `What the Authority must do about this expense`
`Will the Authority pay for this` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the kind of treatment or care` EQUALS `something else` THEN `the Authority is not required to pay`
           IF `the regulations declare it excluded` THEN `no expense is payable for it`
           IF (NOT `it is in my assessed treatment and care needs`) THEN `no expense is payable for it`
           IF (NOT `I was a participant when the expense was incurred`) THEN `the Authority is not required to pay`
           IF (NOT `the expense is reasonable`) THEN `the Act does not say`
           IF `it was provided free` OR (`an approved provider is required` AND (NOT `the provider was approved at the time`)) THEN `the section 11B answer`
           OTHERWISE `the Authority must pay the reasonable expense`
    WHERE
        `an approved provider is required` MEANS
            IF `the kind of treatment or care` EQUALS `attendant care services`
            THEN TRUE
            ELSE `the LTCS Guidelines require an approved provider for it` AND (NOT `it was provided by a medical practitioner`)
        `the section 11B answer` MEANS
            IF `the Authority is of the opinion that special circumstances justify paying`
            THEN `the Authority is not required to pay, but may elect to because it is of the opinion that special circumstances justify it`
            ELSE `the Authority is not required to pay`

-- s 11AA(2) "The Authority's contribution to alternative expenditure is limited to the amount of a reasonable
-- contribution to that expenditure and is not to exceed the amount for which the Authority would otherwise have been
-- liable". The option and the reasonable amount are the Authority's.
@export If the Authority chooses to contribute to an alternative, cost-effective way of meeting my needs, what is the most it will contribute (s 11AA(2))?
GIVEN `a reasonable contribution` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of a reasonable contribution to the alternative expenditure, as the Authority assesses it, in dollars
      `what the Authority would otherwise pay` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the Authority would otherwise have been liable to pay for the expenses of those assessed needs, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most the Authority will contribute to alternative expenditure` MEANS
    `the smaller of` `a reasonable contribution` `and` `what the Authority would otherwise pay`

§§ `Part 3 and Part 4 -- disputes`

-- s 14(1), (2) eligibility disputes to an Assessment Panel, referred by the Authority, the injured person or the insurer;
-- s 20(1), (3) a dispute about whether an injury is a motor accident injury, at an interested person's request, referred
-- by the Authority to the Personal Injury Commission (s 20(2)(a): the person whose injury is the subject of the decision
-- is an interested person, as are the insurer and the Nominal Defendant, (b), (c)); s 24(1) a dispute about the Authority's assessment of treatment and
-- care needs, referred by the Authority to an assessor at the participant's request.
@export Where does my dispute about the Scheme go, and who refers it (ss 14, 20, 24)?
GIVEN `what my dispute is about` IS A `What my dispute is about` @desc What you dispute. One of: "whether my injury meets the eligibility criteria in the LTCS Guidelines", "whether my injury is a motor accident injury", "the Authority's assessment of my treatment and care needs", "something else"
GIVETH A `Where my dispute goes`
`Where does my dispute go` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what my dispute is about`
    WHEN `whether my injury meets the eligibility criteria in the LTCS Guidelines` THEN `to an Assessment Panel of 3 assessors, referred by me, the insurer or the Authority (s 14)`
    WHEN `whether my injury is a motor accident injury` THEN `to the Personal Injury Commission, referred by the Authority at my request (s 20)`
    WHEN `the Authority's assessment of my treatment and care needs` THEN `to an assessor, referred by the Authority if I ask within 28 days after its certificate (s 24)`
    OTHERWISE `the Act sets no dispute process for it`

-- s 15(1) review by a Review Panel "but only on one or more of the following grounds": (a) a change in condition that
-- occurred or first became apparent after the referral and is capable of having a material effect; (b) additional
-- relevant information not available (and not reasonably obtainable) before the referral, capable of having a material
-- effect; (c) not made in accordance with the LTCS Guidelines; (d) demonstrably incorrect in a material respect.
-- s 15(2)(a) the injured person may refer. The Act sets no time limit (finding 4).
@export Can I have the Assessment Panel's determination of my eligibility dispute reviewed by a Review Panel (s 15)?
GIVEN `my condition changed after the referral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your condition changed, or a change first became apparent, after the dispute was referred to the Assessment Panel
      `there is new information that could not have been obtained before the referral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is additional relevant information about the injury that was not available, and could not reasonably have been obtained, before the dispute was referred to the Assessment Panel
      `the change or information could materially affect the determination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that change or information is capable of having a material effect on the determination
      `the determination was not made in accordance with the LTCS Guidelines` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the determination was not made in accordance with the LTCS Guidelines
      `the determination is demonstrably incorrect in a material respect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the determination is demonstrably incorrect in a material respect
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I have the Assessment Panel's determination reviewed` MEANS
    IF `a ground`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `a new matter` MEANS `my condition changed after the referral` OR `there is new information that could not have been obtained before the referral`
        `a ground` MEANS    (`a new matter` AND `the change or information could materially affect the determination`)
                         OR `the determination was not made in accordance with the LTCS Guidelines`
                         OR `the determination is demonstrably incorrect in a material respect`

-- s 24(1) "the Authority must, at the request of the participant, refer the dispute to an assessor"; s 24(2) "A
-- participant cannot make such a request more than 28 days after the Authority gives the participant a copy of the
-- Authority's certificate of assessment". Written as a rule with time 0 the day the certificate is given, in days: the
-- participant's request within 28 days keeps the right to a referral. (Jurally a power with a time limit, not a duty;
-- the rule models the lapse of the power as the LEST.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Scheme party` `Scheme act`
`s 24(2) -- the participant's request for a referral, within 28 days after the certificate` MEANS
    PARTY `the participant`
    MUST `ask the Authority to refer the dispute to an assessor`
    WITHIN 28
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the participant` BECAUSE "the request was made more than 28 days after the Authority gave the certificate of assessment, so the Authority need not refer the dispute (s 24(2))"

-- s 25(2) "An assessor's determination can be referred for review not later than 28 days after the assessor's
-- certificate of determination is given to the Authority and the participant." Time 0 is the day the certificate is
-- given.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Scheme party` `Scheme act`
`s 25(2) -- the participant's referral for review, within 28 days after the assessor's certificate` MEANS
    PARTY `the participant`
    MUST `refer the assessor's determination for review`
    WITHIN 28
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the participant` BECAUSE "the referral was made more than 28 days after the assessor's certificate was given (s 25(2))"

-- Whether the participant's act on day `the day number` (counted from time 0, the day the certificate is given) is in
-- time under the rule: the rule is run by EVALTRACE on that one event.
GIVEN `the act` IS A `Scheme act`, `the day number` IS A NUMBER, `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Scheme party` `Scheme act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`doing` `the act` `on day` `the day number` `is in time under` `the rule` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the participant` `the act` `the day number`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The last day number on which the act is in time under the rule, found by trying each day from `the day number` on
-- until the rule no longer counts the act as in time: the deadline is taken from the rule's own WITHIN, not restated.
-- (Stops at 3660 days, ten years, so that a rule with no deadline cannot run forever; neither rule here comes near it.)
GIVEN `the act` IS A `Scheme act`, `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Scheme party` `Scheme act`, `the day number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day number for` `the act` `under` `the rule` `trying from day` `the day number` MEANS
    IF `the day number` GREATER THAN 3660
    THEN `the day number`
    ELSE IF `doing` `the act` `on day` `the day number` `is in time under` `the rule`
         THEN `the last day number for` `the act` `under` `the rule` `trying from day` (`the day number` PLUS 1)
         ELSE `the day number` MINUS 1

@export What is the last day on which I can ask the Authority to refer my dispute about its treatment and care needs assessment to an assessor (s 24(2))?
GIVEN `the day the Authority gave me its certificate` IS A DATE @desc The day the Authority gave you a copy of its certificate of assessment of your treatment and care needs
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day to ask for an assessor` MEANS
    `the day the Authority gave me its certificate` `plus days` (`the last day number for` `ask the Authority to refer the dispute to an assessor` `under` `s 24(2) -- the participant's request for a referral, within 28 days after the certificate` `trying from day` 0)

@export If I ask on a given day, must the Authority refer my dispute about its treatment and care needs assessment to an assessor (s 24(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the day the Authority gave me its certificate` IS A DATE @desc The day the Authority gave you a copy of its certificate of assessment of your treatment and care needs
      `the day I ask` IS A DATE @desc The day you ask (or asked) the Authority to refer the dispute
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must the Authority refer my dispute to an assessor` MEANS
    IF `the day I ask` `is before` `the day the Authority gave me its certificate`
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (a request before the certificate: the Act is silent)
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 24(2) -- the participant's request for a referral, within 28 days after the certificate` 0 `the events`
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the events` MEANS LIST (EVENT `the participant` `ask the Authority to refer the dispute to an assessor` (`the days from` `the day the Authority gave me its certificate` `to` `the day I ask`))

@export What is the last day on which I can refer the assessor's determination of my treatment and care needs dispute for review by a Review Panel (s 25(2))?
GIVEN `the day the assessor's certificate was given` IS A DATE @desc The day the assessor's certificate of determination was given to you and the Authority
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day to refer the assessor's determination for review` MEANS
    `the day the assessor's certificate was given` `plus days` (`the last day number for` `refer the assessor's determination for review` `under` `s 25(2) -- the participant's referral for review, within 28 days after the assessor's certificate` `trying from day` 0)

-- s 25(1) "The Authority or a participant can refer an assessor's determination ... for review by a Review Panel, but
-- only on one or more of the following grounds": (a) additional relevant information not available (and not reasonably
-- obtainable) at the time of the determination, capable of having a material effect; (b) not made in accordance with the
-- LTCS Guidelines; (c) demonstrably incorrect in a material respect. s 25(2) the 28 days. In a comment only: s 25(5)
-- "In conducting its review, a Review Panel must take into account any written submissions prepared by or on behalf of
-- the participant that are submitted to the Panel" (the Panel's duty; it gives the participant a right to be heard in
-- writing, but no question here turns on it).
@export Can I refer the assessor's determination of my treatment and care needs dispute for review by a Review Panel on a given day (s 25(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the day the assessor's certificate was given` IS A DATE @desc The day the assessor's certificate of determination was given to you and the Authority
      `the day I refer it` IS A DATE @desc The day you refer (or referred) the determination for review
      `there is new information that could not have been obtained at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is additional relevant information about your treatment and care needs that was not available, and could not reasonably have been obtained, at the time of the assessor's determination, and that is capable of having a material effect on it
      `the determination was not made in accordance with the LTCS Guidelines` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the assessor's determination was not made in accordance with the LTCS Guidelines
      `the determination is demonstrably incorrect in a material respect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the assessor's determination is demonstrably incorrect in a material respect
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I refer the assessor's determination for review` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `a ground`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the day I refer it` `is before` `the day the assessor's certificate was given` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (a referral before the certificate: the Act is silent)
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 25(2) -- the participant's referral for review, within 28 days after the assessor's certificate` 0 `the events`
               WHEN FULFILLED THEN JUST TRUE
               OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `a ground` MEANS `there is new information that could not have been obtained at the time` OR `the determination was not made in accordance with the LTCS Guidelines` OR `the determination is demonstrably incorrect in a material respect`
        `the events` MEANS LIST (EVENT `the participant` `refer the assessor's determination for review` (`the days from` `the day the assessor's certificate was given` `to` `the day I refer it`))

-- s 27 "A participant in the Scheme must comply with any reasonable request made by the Authority or an assessor in
-- connection with an assessment of or dispute about the treatment and care needs of the participant, including a
-- request to undergo a medical examination or other examination by a health professional." No deadline and no
-- consequence in the Act (finding 5). An unreasonable request is outside a duty limited in its own words: NOTHING.
@export As a participant, must I comply with this request from the Authority or an assessor, such as to have a medical examination (s 27)?
GIVEN `I am a participant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a participant in the Scheme
      `it is made in connection with my treatment and care needs assessment or dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the request is made by the Authority or an assessor in connection with an assessment of, or a dispute about, your treatment and care needs
      `the request is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the request is reasonable
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I comply with this request` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `I am a participant`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 27 binds participants; silent on others)
           IF (NOT `it is made in connection with my treatment and care needs assessment or dispute`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (outside the duty's own limit)
           IF `the request is reasonable` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (a duty limited by its own wording, "reasonable request")

§§ `Costs of disputes and assessments`

-- s 17(1) "The costs of determinations and reviews of determinations under this Division are payable by the Authority";
-- s 17(2) they include "the necessary costs and expenses of travel and accommodation incurred by the injured person, and
-- by a parent or other carer of the injured person in order to accompany the injured person, in attending a panel".
-- Other costs (other than legal costs, s 18): NOTHING. Whether a cost is necessary is a judgment, asked.
@export In a dispute about my eligibility, will the Authority pay this cost of attending the Assessment Panel or Review Panel (s 17)?
GIVEN `the cost` IS A `The cost of attending a panel` @desc The cost you are asking about. One of: "my travel and accommodation to attend the panel", "the travel and accommodation of a parent or carer who goes with me", "some other cost"
      `the cost was necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cost was necessary for attending the panel
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Will the Authority pay this cost of attending the panel` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the cost`
    WHEN `some other cost` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (s 17(2) "include": the list is not closed)
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the cost was necessary`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (a grant limited by its own wording, "necessary")

-- s 18(1) "No legal costs are payable by the Authority" for an eligibility dispute; s 21(2) "The Authority is to pay
-- those reasonable legal costs of the injured person as assessed by the Commission" for a motor accident injury
-- dispute; s 29(1) "No legal costs are payable by the Authority" for an assessment or a dispute or review about it.
@export Will the Authority pay my legal costs of this Scheme proceeding (ss 18, 21, 29)?
GIVEN `the proceeding` IS A `The proceeding my legal costs are for` @desc The proceeding your legal costs are for. One of: "a dispute about eligibility before an Assessment Panel or Review Panel", "a dispute about whether my injury is a motor accident injury", "an assessment of my treatment and care needs, or a dispute or review about it", "something else"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Will the Authority pay my legal costs` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the proceeding`
    WHEN `a dispute about eligibility before an Assessment Panel or Review Panel` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a dispute about whether my injury is a motor accident injury` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an assessment of my treatment and care needs, or a dispute or review about it` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (the text is silent on other proceedings)

-- s 21(1), (2): the reasonable legal costs as assessed by the Commission; s 21(3), (4): no more than any maximum fixed by
-- the regulations (not deposited: asked). Fork F13: s 21(4) is addressed to the legal practitioner ("is not entitled to
-- be paid or recover"), not to the Authority; the cap is applied to the Authority's payment because s 21(1) and (2)
-- measure it by the costs "payable by the injured person", which cannot exceed what the practitioner may recover, and
-- s 21(6) makes any costs assessment give effect to the regulation. The other reading: the Authority pays the
-- Commission's figure as it stands, and s 21(4) only limits what the practitioner may take.
@export In a dispute about whether my injury is a motor accident injury, how much of my legal costs will the Authority pay (s 21)?
GIVEN `my reasonable legal costs as assessed by the Commission` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of your reasonable legal costs as the Personal Injury Commission assessed them in its determination, in dollars
      `the regulations fix a maximum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations fix maximum legal costs for the legal services concerned
      `the maximum fixed` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum the regulations fix, in dollars (any number if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my legal costs will the Authority pay` MEANS
    IF `the regulations fix a maximum`
    THEN `the smaller of` `my reasonable legal costs as assessed by the Commission` `and` `the maximum fixed`
    ELSE `my reasonable legal costs as assessed by the Commission`
